cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CNVRock, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CNVRock: AMR gene copy-number variation in Klebsiella pneumoniae using variational autoencoders"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2025"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lcerdeira/CNVRock"

authors:
  - family-names: Cerdeira
    given-names: Louise
    affiliation: "London School of Hygiene & Tropical Medicine"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # replace with your ORCID

abstract: >
  CNVRock detects antimicrobial resistance gene copy-number variation in
  Klebsiella pneumoniae Species Complex (KpSC) whole-genome sequencing data.
  A convolutional variational autoencoder learns a low-dimensional
  representation of genome-wide read depth; a Gaussian HMM segments latent
  trajectories into copy-number states; gene-specific callers convert those
  states into per-gene calls for both chromosomal genes (blaSHV) and
  plasmid-borne resistance genes (blaKPC, blaNDM, blaCTX-M, qnrB, blaOXA-48,
  aac(6')-Ib-cr). Applied to 547 KpSC short-read samples from the
  AllTheBacteria catalog, CNVRock achieves MCC ≥ 0.82 across all evaluated
  genes.

keywords:
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - copy number variation
  - Klebsiella pneumoniae
  - variational autoencoder
  - whole genome sequencing
  - plasmid copy number

references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "AllTheBacteria"
    url: "https://www.allthebacteria.org/"
  - type: software
    title: "AMRFinder+"
    url: "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pathogens/antimicrobial-resistance/AMRFinder/"
  - type: software
    title: "Kleborate"
    url: "https://github.com/klebgenomics/Kleborate"
